import Bootstrap.SporosVmWitness

/-!
# Native x86-64 `sporos_vm` Formal Verification Umbrella (`SporosVmBin`)

Top-level umbrella module exporting the complete machine-checked verification
chain for the committed `12,945`-byte native x86-64 Sporos bytecode VM
(`bootstrap/model/sporos_vm`, generated by `bootstrap/model/sporos_vm_gen.cpp`,
with Format A listing `bootstrap/model/sporos_vm.hex` matching
`seed-a < sporos_vm.hex == sporos_vm`):

1. **Exact Binary Decode (`SporosVmCore.table_ok`)**: every instruction in
   `SporosVmBin.vmTable` decodes directly from the committed `SporosVmBin.vmBytes`
   (byte-equality against `bootstrap/model/sporos_vm` verified by
   `Bootstrap/SporosVmCheckBytes.lean`).
2. **Non-Vacuity (`SporosVmReady.mkVmReadyState_rel`)**: for any program
   satisfying `FlatProgFit` and fitting below `2^47`, the concrete post-boot
   state `mkVmReadyState` satisfies `VmRel` with `SporosProvLen.linit`.
3. **Full Simulation (`SporosVmSim.sporos_vm_step_sim`, `sporos_vm_lrun_sim`,
   `sporos_vm_sim_noPhys`, `sporos_vm_sim_noPhys_noNomem`)**: executing
   `vmImage` from any `VmRel`-related state simulates `SporosProvLen.lrun` and
   `Sporos.run pr Sporos.noPhys` across all 14 `Sporos.Instr` constructors
   (all 57 primitives + 8 data/stack/local ops + 5 control-flow ops), matching
   exit status and stdout bytes (modulo oracle `.nomem` exit 2 when memory
   refusal is permitted, and unconditionally when the oracle has no `.nomem`).
4. **Checked-Program Safety (`SporosVmSim.sporos_vm_sim_checked_no_static_fail`)**:
   composes with `Sporos.run_safe` / `SporosProvLen.lrun_safe` so any program
   accepted by `Sporos.checkProg` never hits a static checker error.
5. **TMR Majority-Vote Safety & Quantitative Bound
   (`SporosVmFault.sporos_vm_dispatch_tmr_safe`, `all_inline_voters_ok`,
   `vm_dispatch_tri_phys_bound`)**: every triplicated code-table read and the
   shared dispatch voter `L_vm_vote` masks any single-replica disturbance via
   2-of-3 majority vote and traps 3-way disagreement with exit code 3, with an
   explicit `PDist.fm` bound under `X86Vm.Rates`.
   - **Scope**: TMR covers the triplicated bytecode buffers (`code1`/`code2`/
     `code3`) across dispatch and all inline voters (`allInlineVoterAddrs`);
     unvoted disturbances to host registers, kernel memory, data/return stacks,
     or the VM text segment itself are outside the voter's masking boundary.
6. **Ground Witnesses (`SporosVmWitness`)**: concrete end-to-end execution
   witnesses for `echo`, `hello`, `upper`, `fib`, `provDemo` (both ok paths and
   `demand` failure), plus ground TMR single-disturbance masking and 3-way
   disagreement exit-3 witnesses.

Root A framing: Root A is MUSE's hand-written checker
(`bootstrap/roots/sporos/sporos-stage1.hex`), `spr1_check` is an independent
second check (not Root A or Root A's trust base), and `sporos_vm` is the
post-admission native x86-64 VM paired with `Sporos.decode` + `Sporos.checkProg`.
-/

namespace SporosVmBin

export SporosVmCore (table_ok)
export SporosVmReady (mkVmReadyCtx mkVmReadyState mkVmReadyState_rel)
export SporosVmSim (sporos_vm_step_sim sporos_vm_lrun_sim sporos_vm_sim_noPhys
  sporos_vm_sim_noPhys_noNomem sporos_vm_sim_checked_no_static_fail
  not_hitsNomem_of_no_nomem)
export SporosVmFault (sporos_vm_dispatch_tmr_safe all_inline_voters_ok
  vm_dispatch_tri_phys_bound L_vm_vote_majority_spec L_vm_vote_disagree_spec)
export SporosVmWitness (witness_vm_echo witness_vm_hello witness_vm_upper
  witness_vm_fib witness_vm_provDemo_nonzero witness_vm_provDemo_zero
  witness_vm_provDemo_demand_fail witness_tmr_vote_single_disturbance
  witness_tmr_vote_three_way_exit3)

end SporosVmBin
